    ValueError: Unit Mismatch: conformability error

and most of us can read the traceback and see both the offending line and what
the error is:  multiplying the number of cats by a mass rate for dogs.

We're calling these important strings "semantic units" because they capture
key information about the problem that has been missing from essentially all
the compilers and interpreters.  While there are add-on unit libraries in the
various langμAges, I'd like to make the case that this should be built into
the computing engine at the core level -- it's what I've wanted for decades.
It should be part of every calculation.  A famous units failure was the 1999
Mars Climate Orbiter which crashed and was a loss of about half a billion
dollars in 2026 money.  An older units failure was told by doctor friends of
mine about the confounding of "gr" in prescriptions, which could be
interpreted as either grams or grains, leading to a 15 times under-dosage or
over-dosage, neither of benefit to the patient.  Mike made an important
observation:  this isn't just for physics; an ERP system could use this to
prevent a million-dollar reconciliation error by ensuring "Unit_Price" and
"Quantity" don't get swapped.

